# the row of Reflect.construct forwards the call as a construction. Its code in line constructs, and misses on what the built-in refuses: there the call is made as it is written. The two meet again.
# With fewer operands than the row names, the call stays as it is written.
# RUN: walk f2 f3 f5 mechanisms=none
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: b0([[target]]: {{*}}, [[list]]: {{*}}, [[newTarget]]:
# CHECK: TryCallInline -, [[target]], [[list]], [[newTarget]] inlineBuiltin=ReflectConstruct {{*}}-> done [[done]](), miss [[miss]]()
# CHECK: [[done]]([[constructed]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Jump -> next [[join]]([[constructed]])
# CHECK: [[miss]]() frequency=Rare:
# CHECK: [[called]]: {{*}} = Call {{*}}, [[target]], [[list]], [[newTarget]] calleeName="Reflect.construct"
# CHECK-NEXT: Jump -> next [[join]]([[called]])
# CHECK: [[join]]([[result]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Return [[result]]
# CHECK-LABEL: code f3:Body
# CHECK: TryCallInline
# CHECK-NOT: ReturnCall
# CHECK-LABEL: code f5:Body
# CHECK-NOT: TryCallInline
# CHECK: = Call
# CHECK-NOT: TryCallInline
# RUN(ALL): walk f1 f2 f3 f4
# ALL-COUNT-4: TryCallInline
# ALL-NOT: TryCallInline
# RUN(NEVER): walk f1 f2 f3 f4 f5
# NEVER-NOT: CallBuiltin
# PROGRAM-OF: ../../answers/reflect-construct-done-in-place-constructs-its-target.ir
